{
    "UniqueID": "Tgr_HW_FleasCompanion",
    "//FleasCompanion": "Fleas and lice source 4 of 4 (Documentation/Research/HarshWilds/afflictions.md sections 2.1, 2.2 and 2.4, the first fleas DECISION): keeping an animal companion. The one stat gate is a StatChangeTrigger entry, hw_switch_fleasandlice {1,1} (an unresolved trigger stat fails closed). The companion is the non-stat gate, RequiredCardsOnBoard, one action per companion because every entry of that array must hold (AND): vanilla DogFriend (e20e89c6581b26a4a88ce4b9b7826e5f) and the Sirus23 Mod Collection's tamed companions fc_wolf_companion and fc_fox_companion (UniqueIDs read from Sirus23_Mod_Collection/Patcher/WolfTickPatch.cs and its CardData/Item/WolfCompanion.json and FoxCompanion.json). A companion is a card with the player, so CardIsOnBoard counts it wherever it is carried (ExcludeInventories false). SIRUS23 IS OPTIONAL: with it absent those two UIDs resolve to nothing (WarpResolver returns null for an unresolved UniqueIDScriptable and names it in one Info line, it never makes a stub), and GameManager.CardIsOnBoard returns false for a null card on both of its paths, so a non-inverted entry fails CLOSED and those two actions never play (static reading; harness probe P2 confirms it live). No code works around that and none is needed. RepeatOptions 0 (Repeat), ActionCooldown 96 and OncePerTick: one roll a game day per companion present. Roll: Nothing (weight HW_FLEAS_PET_NOTHING = 19, one card-less drop) against Fleas (weight 1, a card-less drop too), 1 in 20 a day. The Fleas collection adds HW_FLEAS_PER_INFEST = 96 to hw_fleas. Each ActionName.DefaultText is its action's save-state key: unique here, never renamed after release. Every number is a TUNABLE PLACEHOLDER, session-inferred and unmeasured against play (harness probe P3).",
